<title>USA: U.S. Senate retains crop inusrance for tobacco.</title>
<headline>U.S. Senate retains crop inusrance for tobacco.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Senate defeated, 53-47, an amendment on Wednesday to ban crop insurance for tobacco growers.</p>
<p>Opponents said the ban, proposed by Senator Dick Durbin, an Illinois Democrat, would hurt farmers but do nothing for Durbin's longtime goal to reducing tobacco use.</p>
<p>For his part, Durbin said tobacco was &quot;perfectly legal and perfectly lethal. Let's get our health policy and subsidy policy straight.&quot;</p>
<p>Durbin estimated the federal subsidy on crop insurance for tobacco was about $60 million.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
</text>
